1
00:00:05,005 --> 00:00:08,924
Could you please take
Ms. Minamida off the case going forward?

2
00:00:08,925 --> 00:00:10,592
<i>I don't mind.</i>

3
00:00:10,593 --> 00:00:12,177
<i>I can't help...</i>

4
00:00:12,178 --> 00:00:13,763
<i>the defendant.</i>

5
00:00:14,556 --> 00:00:16,224
Ms. Minamida...

6
00:00:17,225 --> 00:00:19,602
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

7
00:00:30,405 --> 00:00:31,655
It's been three days?

8
00:00:31,656 --> 00:00:33,283
Four days.

9
00:00:48,089 --> 00:00:49,256
ATTORNEY MINAMI MINAMIDA

10
00:00:49,257 --> 00:00:52,135
MS. MINAMIDA, ARE YOU OFF TODAY?
HAVEN'T HEARD FROM YOU. ARE YOU OKAY?

11
00:00:59,642 --> 00:01:03,813
HOUSE-ROASTED COFFEE

12
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:18,952
Is this really your old,
run-down family home, Ririi?

13
00:01:18,953 --> 00:01:20,537
We figured we'd make the most

14
00:01:20,538 --> 00:01:23,373
of its age and wear
when turning it into a cafe.

15
00:01:23,374 --> 00:01:26,752
You're opening next month? I'm envious.

16
00:01:26,753 --> 00:01:30,839
Retiring and opening a cafe
in an old house, just the way you want it.

17
00:01:30,840 --> 00:01:32,341
It's always been my dream.

18
00:01:32,342 --> 00:01:35,260
I got carried away with the details,
so money's a little tight.

19
00:01:35,261 --> 00:01:39,182
These are trial dishes. Help yourselves.

20
00:01:40,183 --> 00:01:44,937
We have <i>anmitsu</i> and milk jelly,
both made with agar.

21
00:01:44,938 --> 00:01:47,439
And soft red bean jelly made with agar.

22
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:52,277
And seaweed jelly noodles with
<i>mozuku</i> seaweed or vinegar-miso sauce.

23
00:01:52,278 --> 00:01:53,779
Agar in everything!

24
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:56,616
The Madokas' agar is homemade
by Ririi's mother.

25
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:58,368
Well, time to dig in.

26
00:02:01,663 --> 00:02:03,038
Delicious!

27
00:02:03,039 --> 00:02:05,374
Great desserts in a beautiful setting.

28
00:02:05,375 --> 00:02:06,959
What could be better?

29
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:07,877
Right?

30
00:02:12,006 --> 00:02:14,134
If only that weren't there...

31
00:02:17,428 --> 00:02:19,430
That storage shed's been there forever.

32
00:02:20,098 --> 00:02:21,349
Why not get rid of it?

33
00:02:21,891 --> 00:02:23,142
We can't.

34
00:02:23,143 --> 00:02:24,768
The land is ours,

35
00:02:24,769 --> 00:02:26,437
but the shed belongs to a neighbor.

36
00:02:26,938 --> 00:02:29,273
There used to be
a construction company behind us.

37
00:02:29,274 --> 00:02:32,986
It started using the space
to store materials temporarily.

38
00:02:34,070 --> 00:02:36,947
The owner died four years ago.

39
00:02:36,948 --> 00:02:38,991
When we wanted it removed,

40
00:02:38,992 --> 00:02:40,994
we didn't even know who to contact.

41
00:02:41,911 --> 00:02:45,706
So your land is being occupied unlawfully?

42
00:02:45,707 --> 00:02:47,584
Exactly! Unlawful occupation!

43
00:02:53,798 --> 00:02:55,091
She quit?

44
00:03:01,848 --> 00:03:03,766
She was taken off a case.

45
00:03:04,392 --> 00:03:06,310
I think it shook her confidence.

46
00:03:06,311 --> 00:03:08,062
You should've told me.

47
00:03:12,191 --> 00:03:13,775
I know.

48
00:03:13,776 --> 00:03:15,695
I've got a great idea.

49
00:03:16,654 --> 00:03:18,864
I'll get Minami back on her feet.

50
00:03:18,865 --> 00:03:20,074
Help me out, Mr. Minamida.

51
00:03:24,078 --> 00:03:26,747
I asked around.
It depends on what's stored inside,

52
00:03:26,748 --> 00:03:30,292
but tearing it down and disposing of it
will cost at least 500,000 yen.

53
00:03:30,293 --> 00:03:35,298
Five hundred thousand is a lot
right after a renovation.

54
00:03:35,924 --> 00:03:36,758
Right, Minami?

55
00:03:38,134 --> 00:03:39,635
This roof is handy

56
00:03:39,636 --> 00:03:41,762
for drying agar, though.

57
00:03:41,763 --> 00:03:43,013
Forget about agar for now.

58
00:03:43,014 --> 00:03:44,890
We'll discuss agar later.

59
00:03:44,891 --> 00:03:47,935
We can't dispose of it
without the owner's permission,

60
00:03:47,936 --> 00:03:50,437
but the owner's dead.

61
00:03:50,438 --> 00:03:55,025
Vacant properties
are a serious problem these days.

62
00:03:55,026 --> 00:03:56,444
Right, Minami?

63
00:03:57,570 --> 00:04:01,531
You can quickly look up the heir through
the online property registry service.

64
00:04:01,532 --> 00:04:03,075
Though there is a fee.

65
00:04:03,076 --> 00:04:04,994
That's a practicing lawyer for you!

66
00:04:05,536 --> 00:04:08,205
Let's find the owner
and take him to court. To court!

67
00:04:08,206 --> 00:04:10,582
Isn't going to court a bit much?

68
00:04:10,583 --> 00:04:14,170
Not at all. Right,
Attorney Minami Minamida?

69
00:04:32,355 --> 00:04:34,565
Minami, we'll pay your consultation fee.

70
00:04:35,066 --> 00:04:37,109
- I won't accept a consultation fee.
- But...

71
00:04:37,110 --> 00:04:41,447
I submitted my resignation
to my supervisor and left the firm.

72
00:04:41,948 --> 00:04:44,992
I'm only here because Ririi asked me
to come with her.

73
00:04:44,993 --> 00:04:48,162
Don't be like that.
Your best friend's family needs help.

74
00:04:49,247 --> 00:04:50,081
This is it.

75
00:04:58,006 --> 00:05:00,674
Oh, sure. Go ahead
and remove it if you want.

76
00:05:00,675 --> 00:05:04,594
It's been sitting there since my dad died.
It's basically junk.

77
00:05:04,595 --> 00:05:08,099
Actually, we were hoping you'd arrange
to have it removed.

78
00:05:08,683 --> 00:05:09,976
- What, us?
- Of course.

79
00:05:11,019 --> 00:05:11,977
Why?

80
00:05:11,978 --> 00:05:14,938
You inherited the construction company's
land and building, correct?

81
00:05:14,939 --> 00:05:16,565
That junk

82
00:05:16,566 --> 00:05:20,277
is between my dad and your family.
It has nothing to do with me.

83
00:05:20,278 --> 00:05:21,653
It does involve you.

84
00:05:21,654 --> 00:05:23,280
- No, it doesn't.
- Yes, it does.

85
00:05:23,281 --> 00:05:24,614
- No, it doesn't.
- Yes, it does!

86
00:05:24,615 --> 00:05:25,615
- No!
- Yes!

87
00:05:25,616 --> 00:05:27,034
No!

88
00:05:27,035 --> 00:05:28,744
- It does involve you!
- What?

89
00:05:28,745 --> 00:05:32,039
Mr. Madoka can exercise his right
to reclaim his property.

90
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:33,665
There it is! The right to reclaim it!

91
00:05:33,666 --> 00:05:38,503
If someone else's occupation interferes
with your ownership, you have the right

92
00:05:38,504 --> 00:05:40,756
to demand the property's return.

93
00:05:40,757 --> 00:05:44,885
In this case, the storage shed was built
on Mr. Madoka's land without permission

94
00:05:44,886 --> 00:05:46,636
and occupies that land.

95
00:05:46,637 --> 00:05:48,764
As the heir to Tsugihara Construction's

96
00:05:48,765 --> 00:05:51,308
land and building,
you bear that responsibility.

97
00:05:51,309 --> 00:05:54,394
Mr. Madoka has the right to demand
that you remove the shed

98
00:05:54,395 --> 00:05:55,687
and vacate his land.

99
00:05:55,688 --> 00:05:57,815
See? We have the right!

100
00:05:58,483 --> 00:05:59,484
Who is this woman?

101
00:06:00,985 --> 00:06:04,196
This is Minami Minamida, an attorney.

102
00:06:04,197 --> 00:06:07,199
An attorney? Over some junk?

103
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:10,368
I'm only here because
Ririi asked me to come...

104
00:06:10,369 --> 00:06:13,705
Anyway, it could collapse
and hurt someone,

105
00:06:13,706 --> 00:06:18,085
so please remove it promptly.
Immediately. This second.

106
00:06:18,086 --> 00:06:19,712
In this economy?

107
00:06:20,421 --> 00:06:22,715
Where am I supposed to get
that kind of money?

108
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:24,967
I'm sorry.

109
00:06:30,515 --> 00:06:31,974
Minami!

110
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:35,019
I'm so glad you came, Minami.

111
00:06:39,732 --> 00:06:42,067
I only explained the right
to reclaim property.

112
00:06:42,068 --> 00:06:43,652
I wasn't representing you, Ririi.

113
00:06:43,653 --> 00:06:47,072
Without that reclaim-whatever
you hit him with,

114
00:06:47,073 --> 00:06:49,242
he'd have brushed us off.

115
00:06:49,867 --> 00:06:53,078
Minami, you really should stay a lawyer.

116
00:06:53,079 --> 00:06:54,079
Right, Daddy?

117
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:56,541
Yes. Thank you, Minami.

118
00:07:00,253 --> 00:07:02,171
OPEN
PREPARING TO OPEN

119
00:07:03,339 --> 00:07:04,840
Hello? Anyone here?

120
00:07:04,841 --> 00:07:06,134
Yes?

121
00:07:18,521 --> 00:07:20,564
CREATIVE ONIGIRI SHOP

122
00:07:20,565 --> 00:07:21,482
What do we do?

123
00:07:22,316 --> 00:07:23,316
What's wrong?

124
00:07:23,317 --> 00:07:25,152
Their lawyer showed up.

125
00:07:25,153 --> 00:07:26,112
What?

126
00:07:32,743 --> 00:07:34,202
So this is it...

127
00:07:34,203 --> 00:07:36,955
Yes. It's been here since around
when my daughter was born,

128
00:07:36,956 --> 00:07:38,291
so at least 20 years.

129
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:42,377
Were you renting this land
to Tsugihara Construction?

130
00:07:42,378 --> 00:07:45,255
No. I thought they'd remove it eventually.

131
00:07:45,256 --> 00:07:46,466
You never said anything?

132
00:07:47,091 --> 00:07:49,886
They were our neighbors. It was awkward.

133
00:07:50,553 --> 00:07:51,637
I see.

134
00:07:52,346 --> 00:07:56,142
Then they may qualify for
adverse possession after 20 years.

135
00:07:57,059 --> 00:07:59,102
Adverse possession?

136
00:07:59,103 --> 00:08:01,229
If someone openly and peacefully

137
00:08:01,230 --> 00:08:04,649
occupies land for a certain period,

138
00:08:04,650 --> 00:08:06,735
they can claim ownership of it.

139
00:08:06,736 --> 00:08:08,111
Here,

140
00:08:08,112 --> 00:08:10,780
the shed has occupied the Madokas' land

141
00:08:10,781 --> 00:08:14,534
for over 20 years, satisfying the period

142
00:08:14,535 --> 00:08:16,369
required for adverse possession.

143
00:08:16,370 --> 00:08:19,956
So the land under the shed becomes theirs?

144
00:08:19,957 --> 00:08:22,000
That's not all.

145
00:08:22,001 --> 00:08:23,752
If adverse possession is established,

146
00:08:23,753 --> 00:08:27,172
ownership passes to the Tsugihara side,

147
00:08:27,173 --> 00:08:29,883
so you can no longer
demand removal of the shed.

148
00:08:29,884 --> 00:08:33,011
They've found a tricky point
to use against us.

149
00:08:33,012 --> 00:08:34,721
But how is that fair?

150
00:08:34,722 --> 00:08:37,057
We let them use our land out of kindness.

151
00:08:37,058 --> 00:08:40,894
Apparently, not objecting to their use
of the land for 20 years

152
00:08:40,895 --> 00:08:43,605
counts as accepting
their possession of it.

153
00:08:43,606 --> 00:08:44,899
This is the worst.

154
00:08:45,483 --> 00:08:47,817
Now Daddy's saying he can't open the cafe

155
00:08:47,818 --> 00:08:50,154
with that shed still there.

156
00:08:50,655 --> 00:08:52,489
It's my fault.

157
00:08:52,490 --> 00:08:55,492
Because I brought up the right
to reclaim the property...

158
00:08:55,493 --> 00:08:57,536
It's not your fault, Minami.

159
00:08:57,537 --> 00:08:59,454
I'm the one who asked you to come.

160
00:08:59,455 --> 00:09:02,749
But now that they've hired a lawyer,

161
00:09:02,750 --> 00:09:04,835
we need to figure out how to respond.

162
00:09:06,170 --> 00:09:07,170
I know!

163
00:09:07,171 --> 00:09:09,047
I've stopped being a lawyer,

164
00:09:09,048 --> 00:09:11,925
but I know other lawyers.
I can introduce you to one, Ririi.

165
00:09:11,926 --> 00:09:13,553
You represent me, Minami.

166
00:09:14,679 --> 00:09:15,596
No.

167
00:09:16,097 --> 00:09:18,724
I can't help you, Ririi.

168
00:09:22,853 --> 00:09:24,814
Minami? I'm outside the building.

169
00:09:25,398 --> 00:09:27,023
What do I do again?

170
00:09:27,024 --> 00:09:29,818
First, check in at the entrance.

171
00:09:29,819 --> 00:09:32,112
Right. I just give them your name?

172
00:09:32,113 --> 00:09:34,656
<i>No! I've already left the firm.</i>

173
00:09:34,657 --> 00:09:36,157
I'm sure it'll still work.

174
00:09:36,158 --> 00:09:37,617
Don't use Minami Minamida!

175
00:09:37,618 --> 00:09:40,079
I'll try Minami Minamida.

176
00:09:46,168 --> 00:09:47,128
Excuse me...

177
00:09:47,628 --> 00:09:49,255
Do you know Ms. Minamida?

178
00:09:50,548 --> 00:09:51,798
Do you work at the law firm?

179
00:09:51,799 --> 00:09:53,050
Yes.

180
00:09:53,634 --> 00:09:55,260
<i>Ririi? Are you listening?</i>

181
00:09:55,261 --> 00:09:57,429
<i>Don't say Minami Minamida.</i>

182
00:09:57,430 --> 00:09:59,307
I'll ask someone here. Never mind.

183
00:10:05,688 --> 00:10:06,646
I must decline.

184
00:10:06,647 --> 00:10:08,982
- What? Is that a no?
- Yes.

185
00:10:08,983 --> 00:10:13,654
Minami said this Mr. Miyaji was someone
she could sort of recommend.

186
00:10:22,997 --> 00:10:26,375
Once adverse possession is established,
it's difficult to overturn.

187
00:10:26,876 --> 00:10:30,295
If she wants to take a losing case,
she should handle it herself.

188
00:10:30,296 --> 00:10:31,463
But Minami's already...

189
00:10:31,464 --> 00:10:35,216
Resigning doesn't stop her
from being a lawyer.

190
00:10:35,217 --> 00:10:38,094
What? So Ms. Minamida really did...

191
00:10:38,095 --> 00:10:40,431
So that's why she hasn't been coming in.

192
00:10:41,223 --> 00:10:42,641
Well...

193
00:10:42,642 --> 00:10:43,892
To be precise,

194
00:10:43,893 --> 00:10:47,897
she just left a resignation letter
on my desk without discussing it with me.

195
00:10:49,106 --> 00:10:50,982
Isn't there some way we could help?

196
00:10:50,983 --> 00:10:52,026
I'm afraid not.

197
00:10:57,865 --> 00:11:00,742
I came all this way for nothing.

198
00:11:00,743 --> 00:11:02,828
I'm sorry we couldn't help.

199
00:11:03,412 --> 00:11:04,955
Is something wrong?

200
00:11:06,082 --> 00:11:07,083
Managing Partner.

201
00:11:07,625 --> 00:11:08,459
Managing Partner?

202
00:11:11,921 --> 00:11:14,214
- Why not take her case?
- But...

203
00:11:14,215 --> 00:11:16,716
Ms. Minamida came to us

204
00:11:16,717 --> 00:11:18,176
because she trusts the team

205
00:11:18,177 --> 00:11:21,179
she worked with, however briefly.
Isn't that right?

206
00:11:21,180 --> 00:11:22,889
If she trusted us, would she have left

207
00:11:22,890 --> 00:11:25,558
without a word to her supervisor
or colleagues?

208
00:11:25,559 --> 00:11:28,312
She'll tell us when she's ready.

209
00:11:28,979 --> 00:11:32,357
We all have strengths and weaknesses.
We support each other.

210
00:11:32,358 --> 00:11:34,485
Isn't that how a team should work?

211
00:11:37,446 --> 00:11:38,739
A team...

212
00:11:40,282 --> 00:11:43,285
All right. If you feel
that strongly about it.

213
00:11:44,245 --> 00:11:46,455
But I have one condition.

214
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:53,420
So why am I the one handling it?

215
00:11:53,421 --> 00:11:56,548
Mr. Miyaji and Mr. Himi
both seem to have heavy caseloads.

216
00:11:56,549 --> 00:11:58,383
I have a pretty heavy caseload myself.

217
00:11:58,384 --> 00:11:59,301
Yes.

218
00:11:59,885 --> 00:12:02,929
Well, when she became my colleague,

219
00:12:02,930 --> 00:12:06,350
I knew she'd give me
the runaround sometimes...

220
00:12:06,851 --> 00:12:08,561
Suwa, huh...

221
00:12:09,770 --> 00:12:11,647
Would you like me to drive you?

222
00:12:16,235 --> 00:12:20,030
Suwa... It's a lovely place, isn't it?

223
00:12:23,033 --> 00:12:25,202
NEW! AGAR RICE BALLS ¥560
HIGH IN FIBER! HEALTHIER!

224
00:12:45,389 --> 00:12:46,348
Minami.

225
00:12:53,731 --> 00:12:54,565
Minami!

226
00:12:56,358 --> 00:12:59,153
Don't "hm?" me. You're working.

227
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:02,572
If it's on your mind,

228
00:13:02,573 --> 00:13:04,867
why don't you join them
for the negotiations?

229
00:13:08,245 --> 00:13:09,787
I think Ririi would be happy

230
00:13:09,788 --> 00:13:12,082
to have you represent her.

231
00:13:25,471 --> 00:13:28,515
<i>Were you renting this land
to Tsugihara Construction?</i>

232
00:13:28,516 --> 00:13:31,684
<i>No. I thought they'd remove it eventually.</i>

233
00:13:31,685 --> 00:13:32,894
<i>You never said anything?</i>

234
00:13:32,895 --> 00:13:35,940
<i>They were our neighbors. It was awkward.</i>

235
00:13:37,691 --> 00:13:40,152
That's my conversation
with Mr. Madoka the other day.

236
00:13:40,945 --> 00:13:42,238
That's accurate, correct?

237
00:13:42,863 --> 00:13:43,821
Yes.

238
00:13:43,822 --> 00:13:46,408
So you admit to adverse possession?

239
00:13:48,911 --> 00:13:50,204
About that,

240
00:13:50,788 --> 00:13:54,290
if you're taking this position

241
00:13:54,291 --> 00:13:56,627
because our demand
the other day offended you,

242
00:13:57,127 --> 00:13:58,379
we apologize.

243
00:14:02,841 --> 00:14:05,051
We'll do what we can

244
00:14:05,052 --> 00:14:07,845
to help remove the shed.

245
00:14:07,846 --> 00:14:10,683
Would you consider withdrawing
your adverse possession claim?

246
00:14:11,433 --> 00:14:13,519
You'll do what you can?

247
00:14:14,937 --> 00:14:15,771
What do you think?

248
00:14:25,573 --> 00:14:27,574
What did Ririi say?

249
00:14:27,575 --> 00:14:30,244
They wouldn't withdraw
their adverse possession claim.

250
00:14:31,579 --> 00:14:33,037
I see.

251
00:14:33,038 --> 00:14:35,498
Isn't there something we can do?

252
00:14:35,499 --> 00:14:39,961
Many people feel too awkward to ask others
to return what they've borrowed.

253
00:14:39,962 --> 00:14:42,463
Even that jacket I always wear

254
00:14:42,464 --> 00:14:44,008
wasn't originally mine.

255
00:14:44,550 --> 00:14:47,552
That must've been
about 20 years ago, actually.

256
00:14:47,553 --> 00:14:50,597
I got drunk at a school reunion
and wore it home by mistake.

257
00:14:50,598 --> 00:14:52,016
And I've had it ever since.

258
00:14:52,892 --> 00:14:55,226
Didn't the owner ask you to return it?

259
00:14:55,227 --> 00:14:58,981
No. He'd gone home
wearing my leather jacket.

260
00:15:00,190 --> 00:15:04,278
So adverse possession
applies to both of us, right?

261
00:15:06,488 --> 00:15:09,074
Adverse possession applies to both...

262
00:15:11,285 --> 00:15:15,163
Could adverse possession
apply to the Madokas too,

263
00:15:15,164 --> 00:15:16,498
not just them?

264
00:15:37,478 --> 00:15:38,686
This is good.

265
00:15:38,687 --> 00:15:39,897
Right?

266
00:15:48,739 --> 00:15:49,572
Yes.

267
00:15:49,573 --> 00:15:53,285
<i>Hello. I'm Makoto, Minami's father.</i>

268
00:15:53,953 --> 00:15:54,828
Huh?

269
00:15:56,997 --> 00:15:59,792
Civil law recognizes
two types of prescription:

270
00:16:00,334 --> 00:16:02,710
acquisitive prescription,
which grants rights,

271
00:16:02,711 --> 00:16:05,172
and extinctive prescription,
which extinguishes them.

272
00:16:06,674 --> 00:16:07,632
<i>The key here</i>

273
00:16:07,633 --> 00:16:10,052
<i>is adverse possession.</i>

274
00:16:11,261 --> 00:16:14,138
The key here is adverse possession.

275
00:16:14,139 --> 00:16:16,432
This is way too much hassle!

276
00:16:16,433 --> 00:16:17,518
Um...

277
00:16:18,686 --> 00:16:19,727
Do it yourself!

278
00:16:19,728 --> 00:16:21,145
But I...

279
00:16:21,146 --> 00:16:23,606
Just talk to her yourself! Come on!

280
00:16:23,607 --> 00:16:24,608
Ms. Minamida?

281
00:16:30,406 --> 00:16:31,615
Yes.

282
00:16:32,282 --> 00:16:34,075
It's a long shot,

283
00:16:34,076 --> 00:16:36,495
but there may be a way to make this work.

284
00:16:39,957 --> 00:16:42,250
Mr. Tsugihara has acquired
the Madokas' land

285
00:16:42,251 --> 00:16:45,253
<i>by adverse possession</i>

286
00:16:45,254 --> 00:16:47,548
through continuing to occupy it
as his own.

287
00:16:48,382 --> 00:16:52,261
But couldn't the same argument
work the other way around?

288
00:16:53,012 --> 00:16:53,928
The other way around?

289
00:16:53,929 --> 00:16:57,932
In other words, we could argue
that the Madokas

290
00:16:57,933 --> 00:17:01,729
have possessed the shed
on their land for 20 years.

291
00:17:02,896 --> 00:17:04,689
I see.

292
00:17:04,690 --> 00:17:07,191
If the shed belongs to the Madokas,

293
00:17:07,192 --> 00:17:11,029
Mr. Tsugihara would no longer have grounds
to claim the land as his own.

294
00:17:11,030 --> 00:17:12,280
Yes.

295
00:17:12,281 --> 00:17:16,451
The Madokas would have to dispose
of the shed themselves,

296
00:17:16,452 --> 00:17:18,871
but they could avoid losing their land.

297
00:17:19,747 --> 00:17:21,956
That may work in theory,

298
00:17:21,957 --> 00:17:24,959
but both sides would be using
the same law in the same dispute.

299
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:27,170
One would claim the land,

300
00:17:27,171 --> 00:17:29,797
and the other the shed.

301
00:17:29,798 --> 00:17:32,092
Which claim would prevail?

302
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:34,218
Probably

303
00:17:34,219 --> 00:17:37,931
whichever side can provide
clearer evidence of possession.

304
00:17:38,515 --> 00:17:42,853
What would prove they've possessed
the shed for 20 years?

305
00:17:44,146 --> 00:17:45,439
That would be...

306
00:17:49,485 --> 00:17:51,195
The agar!

307
00:17:52,071 --> 00:17:53,112
Yes!

308
00:17:53,113 --> 00:17:54,781
Every year, Ririi's mother

309
00:17:54,782 --> 00:17:56,657
dried seaweed on the shed's roof

310
00:17:56,658 --> 00:17:58,743
to make her own agar.

311
00:17:58,744 --> 00:18:03,247
That would support the Madokas' claim
to 20 years' possession of the shed.

312
00:18:03,248 --> 00:18:04,624
She did! Every year!

313
00:18:04,625 --> 00:18:06,459
Can you prove that?

314
00:18:06,460 --> 00:18:10,088
Are there any photos,
or perhaps entries in your mother's diary?

315
00:18:10,089 --> 00:18:12,925
My parents aren't the type
to take photos or keep diaries.

316
00:18:17,304 --> 00:18:18,347
What about sketches?

317
00:18:22,101 --> 00:18:24,393
I've loved drawing since I was little.

318
00:18:24,394 --> 00:18:26,229
I used to draw the garden a lot.

319
00:18:26,230 --> 00:18:29,149
Wow, these are good!

320
00:18:30,567 --> 00:18:33,737
It's amazing what your parents keep.

321
00:18:38,534 --> 00:18:42,746
You can go help Ririi, you know.

322
00:18:47,417 --> 00:18:49,503
I have to help here at the shop.

323
00:18:56,552 --> 00:18:59,053
I think there are more
of Ririi's drawings upstairs.

324
00:18:59,054 --> 00:19:00,680
Could we see them?

325
00:19:00,681 --> 00:19:01,849
Please.

326
00:19:11,066 --> 00:19:13,360
Um, is the person in this drawing...?

327
00:19:14,653 --> 00:19:16,779
Yeah, that's Minami in middle school.

328
00:19:16,780 --> 00:19:18,490
Oh, wow.

329
00:19:19,491 --> 00:19:22,911
What was Ms. Minamida like back then?

330
00:19:23,620 --> 00:19:26,290
The kids in our class
called her "Miss Okay."

331
00:19:26,874 --> 00:19:28,083
"Miss Okay"?

332
00:19:29,501 --> 00:19:31,169
Minami transferred to our school...

333
00:19:31,170 --> 00:19:35,256
I'd like to introduce a student
who's joining our class today.

334
00:19:35,257 --> 00:19:37,216
Could you introduce yourself?

335
00:19:37,217 --> 00:19:41,846
Yes! Forwards or backwards,
I'm Minami Minamida!

336
00:19:41,847 --> 00:19:43,849
Kayak, deed... Oh...

337
00:19:44,558 --> 00:19:45,392
What's wrong?

338
00:19:45,976 --> 00:19:48,102
My father told me not to say

339
00:19:48,103 --> 00:19:52,816
anything unnecessary when introducing
myself at my new school, but I did.

340
00:19:54,693 --> 00:19:56,570
All right, quiet down!

341
00:19:57,154 --> 00:19:59,614
Minamida, take that seat over there.

342
00:19:59,615 --> 00:20:00,949
Yes.

343
00:20:01,867 --> 00:20:03,869
All right, settle down.

344
00:20:04,578 --> 00:20:05,828
Let's start homeroom.

345
00:20:05,829 --> 00:20:09,082
<i>At first, I just thought the new girl
seemed kind of slow.</i>

346
00:20:12,085 --> 00:20:14,004
<i>She was always falling over.</i>

347
00:20:17,883 --> 00:20:19,800
Huh? What happened?

348
00:20:19,801 --> 00:20:22,721
Hey, Minamida, are you okay?

349
00:20:23,555 --> 00:20:24,556
Hey...

350
00:20:25,057 --> 00:20:26,141
I'm okay...

351
00:20:27,601 --> 00:20:28,852
<i>And bumping into things.</i>

352
00:20:36,818 --> 00:20:38,527
That must hurt!

353
00:20:38,528 --> 00:20:39,779
Are you okay?

354
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:41,114
I'm okay.

355
00:20:41,907 --> 00:20:43,116
Come on, let's go.

356
00:20:45,244 --> 00:20:49,206
<i>She always echoed "okay,"
so they called her "Miss Okay."</i>

357
00:20:50,666 --> 00:20:53,210
<i>But I hadn't realized.</i>

358
00:20:58,048 --> 00:21:00,259
What will she say
if someone bumps into her?

359
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:02,802
Let's find out.

360
00:21:02,803 --> 00:21:03,887
Go for it!

361
00:21:09,559 --> 00:21:12,813
Miss Okay's rice ball rolled away.

362
00:21:13,480 --> 00:21:15,106
Are you okay?

363
00:21:15,107 --> 00:21:16,440
I'm okay.

364
00:21:16,441 --> 00:21:18,026
There she goes again.

365
00:21:18,944 --> 00:21:20,278
There she goes again.

366
00:21:20,279 --> 00:21:21,404
That's all she can say.

367
00:21:21,405 --> 00:21:22,698
She's so freaking funny!

368
00:21:23,699 --> 00:21:26,159
<i>It was all just their stupid idea of fun.</i>

369
00:21:28,537 --> 00:21:30,204
That was seriously hilarious!

370
00:21:30,205 --> 00:21:31,706
You're so good at that!

371
00:21:31,707 --> 00:21:33,292
She said she's okay.

372
00:21:34,334 --> 00:21:37,170
- What's she gonna do with that rice ball?
- Good question!

373
00:21:43,802 --> 00:21:47,471
<i>Then I suddenly felt this urge
to get some exercise.</i>

374
00:21:47,472 --> 00:21:48,973
Oh my god, you're too good.

375
00:21:48,974 --> 00:21:50,891
Maybe I'll do it again tomorrow.

376
00:21:50,892 --> 00:21:52,351
- That'd be awesome.
- Awesome!

377
00:21:52,352 --> 00:21:53,520
Right?

378
00:21:59,526 --> 00:22:00,777
Hey! What the hell?!

379
00:22:01,945 --> 00:22:05,614
You're covered in trash. Are you okay?

380
00:22:05,615 --> 00:22:07,116
Are you okay?

381
00:22:07,117 --> 00:22:08,493
No, I'm not okay!

382
00:22:09,953 --> 00:22:11,787
What the hell are you doing?

383
00:22:11,788 --> 00:22:14,041
Stop it! Let go!

384
00:22:23,842 --> 00:22:27,596
Time to sweep out the trash!

385
00:22:39,900 --> 00:22:41,401
All clean now.

386
00:22:42,944 --> 00:22:44,488
All clean now.

387
00:22:45,947 --> 00:22:47,741
<i>Then, the next day...</i>

388
00:23:03,548 --> 00:23:05,300
You're distracting me. Need something?

389
00:23:07,803 --> 00:23:09,846
First period has already started!

390
00:23:11,223 --> 00:23:12,432
So?

391
00:23:37,290 --> 00:23:39,626
I thought we could
walk to school together.

392
00:23:43,255 --> 00:23:45,757
I'm safe when I'm with you, Madoka.

393
00:23:46,633 --> 00:23:48,552
There's nothing in it for me.

394
00:24:01,773 --> 00:24:04,108
Bryde's whales stay upright in the water

395
00:24:04,109 --> 00:24:06,194
with their mouths open,
waiting for food to enter!

396
00:24:06,778 --> 00:24:07,737
Like this.

397
00:24:10,490 --> 00:24:12,032
The benefit for you

398
00:24:12,033 --> 00:24:15,035
is that I can model
for your drawings anytime.

399
00:24:15,036 --> 00:24:17,788
Since you don't seem to have
any friends at school.

400
00:24:17,789 --> 00:24:20,834
I'm alone by choice. It's easier that way.

401
00:24:25,338 --> 00:24:28,800
Then I'll be alone with you.

402
00:24:34,055 --> 00:24:35,682
You're so weird...

403
00:24:39,728 --> 00:24:42,188
Ms. Madoka? Where are you going?

404
00:24:42,189 --> 00:24:45,482
Ririi. No "Miss" or anything. Just Ririi.

405
00:24:45,483 --> 00:24:47,027
Drop the formalities.

406
00:24:49,696 --> 00:24:50,614
Ririi...

407
00:24:51,156 --> 00:24:53,657
I'm going to school. Alone.

408
00:24:53,658 --> 00:24:55,493
No formalities.

409
00:24:57,996 --> 00:24:59,205
Ririi!

410
00:24:59,206 --> 00:25:02,792
I shall... I'll come too! Alone.

411
00:25:07,255 --> 00:25:09,882
We started hanging out after that.

412
00:25:09,883 --> 00:25:12,344
There's never a dull moment with Minami.

413
00:25:14,221 --> 00:25:15,222
I know what you mean.

414
00:25:15,931 --> 00:25:19,726
I lose track of time
when I'm with Ms. Minamida too.

415
00:25:25,440 --> 00:25:28,567
Found them!
She drew these before elementary school.

416
00:25:28,568 --> 00:25:30,903
- Wow! Parents really do keep everything.
- Thank you.

417
00:25:30,904 --> 00:25:32,614
Have some agar jelly.

418
00:25:33,698 --> 00:25:35,741
- Thank you.
- Of course.

419
00:25:35,742 --> 00:25:38,870
Let's have some agar jelly,
then get back to work.

420
00:25:39,996 --> 00:25:41,706
Shall we take an agar jelly break?

421
00:25:42,374 --> 00:25:43,249
I'll have some.

422
00:25:43,250 --> 00:25:45,377
- Looks good!
- Thank you.

423
00:25:46,211 --> 00:25:47,711
The shed

424
00:25:47,712 --> 00:25:49,922
gets just the right amount
of sun and airflow.

425
00:25:49,923 --> 00:25:52,509
It's the perfect place to dry agar.

426
00:25:53,510 --> 00:25:55,344
They shared their agar

427
00:25:55,345 --> 00:25:59,139
with your father every year,
supporting their claim

428
00:25:59,140 --> 00:26:02,060
of peaceful, open possession.

429
00:26:03,436 --> 00:26:04,396
But

430
00:26:04,896 --> 00:26:09,192
isn't it a stretch to claim 20 years
of possession based on a few sketches?

431
00:26:10,110 --> 00:26:12,403
Ultimately, that's for the court
to decide.

432
00:26:12,404 --> 00:26:14,697
Even so, I understand

433
00:26:14,698 --> 00:26:18,702
you initially asked Mr. Tsugihara
to remove the shed.

434
00:26:19,286 --> 00:26:20,287
Yes.

435
00:26:20,787 --> 00:26:25,499
Which means you recognized
Mr. Tsugihara as its owner, correct?

436
00:26:25,500 --> 00:26:29,212
Now you're saying the shed belongs to you.

437
00:26:30,714 --> 00:26:32,757
That's a contradiction.

438
00:26:33,258 --> 00:26:34,550
You can't change your story now.

439
00:26:34,551 --> 00:26:36,176
You did the same thing!

440
00:26:36,177 --> 00:26:40,514
Yes. Mr. Tsugihara hadn't mentioned
adverse possession then either.

441
00:26:40,515 --> 00:26:42,391
You brought a lawyer first!

442
00:26:42,392 --> 00:26:44,143
That's why we'd like to revisit...

443
00:26:44,144 --> 00:26:45,270
Ms. Asahi!

444
00:26:46,062 --> 00:26:47,522
That's enough.

445
00:26:50,692 --> 00:26:51,901
Let's put an end to this.

446
00:27:16,509 --> 00:27:18,428
So what did Ririi's father decide?

447
00:27:19,054 --> 00:27:21,139
He's giving up ownership of the land.

448
00:27:22,223 --> 00:27:24,808
Going to court would take time and money.

449
00:27:24,809 --> 00:27:26,644
He doesn't want any more conflict.

450
00:27:27,979 --> 00:27:30,606
So the shed will stay where it is?

451
00:27:30,607 --> 00:27:32,400
Is Ririi okay with that?

452
00:27:33,193 --> 00:27:34,235
No...

453
00:27:35,904 --> 00:27:38,156
I'm sorry I couldn't help.

454
00:27:45,622 --> 00:27:48,665
I'm sorry for all the trouble.

455
00:27:48,666 --> 00:27:52,419
We'll update the property registration
after the survey.

456
00:27:52,420 --> 00:27:54,047
Thank you for handling it.

457
00:27:59,761 --> 00:28:01,388
Why are we the ones apologizing?

458
00:28:07,685 --> 00:28:09,729
Nothing but junk.

459
00:28:14,567 --> 00:28:16,194
Will you clean this up properly?

460
00:28:24,035 --> 00:28:24,953
There we go.

461
00:28:27,997 --> 00:28:30,124
There.

462
00:28:30,125 --> 00:28:31,709
- Let's go.
- Right.

463
00:28:46,808 --> 00:28:48,226
Ririi, look out!

464
00:29:02,449 --> 00:29:03,742
Daddy!

465
00:29:15,754 --> 00:29:17,130
- Ririi!
- Minami.

466
00:29:18,006 --> 00:29:19,548
Are you okay, Mr. Madoka?

467
00:29:19,549 --> 00:29:21,843
Sorry I worried you all.

468
00:29:22,761 --> 00:29:24,971
Bruised all over. A month to recover.

469
00:29:25,638 --> 00:29:27,806
It looks worse than it is.
It's nothing serious.

470
00:29:27,807 --> 00:29:30,768
What are you talking about?
You could've died!

471
00:29:30,769 --> 00:29:34,856
Minami, their shed hurt him.
We can hold them responsible, right?

472
00:29:36,149 --> 00:29:37,024
Well...

473
00:29:37,025 --> 00:29:38,275
Just let it go.

474
00:29:38,276 --> 00:29:40,486
We're finally close to settling this.

475
00:29:40,487 --> 00:29:42,196
We'd only stir things up again.

476
00:29:42,197 --> 00:29:43,364
I'm okay.

477
00:29:43,865 --> 00:29:45,491
You're not okay!

478
00:29:45,492 --> 00:29:47,326
We can't just sweep this under the rug!

479
00:29:47,327 --> 00:29:50,205
Ignoring things is what got us
into this mess!

480
00:29:51,956 --> 00:29:53,082
What about the cafe?

481
00:29:54,250 --> 00:29:55,335
It was your dream!

482
00:29:56,669 --> 00:29:59,756
I don't want my family
getting hurt anymore!

483
00:30:15,230 --> 00:30:16,189
Ririi.

484
00:30:17,440 --> 00:30:18,483
I...

485
00:30:24,572 --> 00:30:25,532
I...

486
00:30:27,116 --> 00:30:28,785
I want to help you, Ririi.

487
00:30:29,911 --> 00:30:31,788
I want to help your family.

488
00:30:37,126 --> 00:30:38,419
Can I do it?

489
00:30:45,051 --> 00:30:47,470
Of course you can.

490
00:30:50,265 --> 00:30:51,808
Even though I'm autistic?

491
00:30:53,726 --> 00:30:57,188
Have I ever cared about that?

492
00:31:09,909 --> 00:31:13,204
Please let me represent your family.

493
00:31:17,584 --> 00:31:18,793
Dear.

494
00:31:19,294 --> 00:31:21,754
Let's face our problems properly.

495
00:31:22,338 --> 00:31:24,464
Shouldn't we establish who's responsible,

496
00:31:24,465 --> 00:31:27,802
if only to protect the people
we care about?

497
00:31:30,054 --> 00:31:33,266
I want to put my trust in Minami.

498
00:31:37,854 --> 00:31:39,147
You're right.

499
00:31:40,899 --> 00:31:42,066
Minami, we'd like your...

500
00:31:43,985 --> 00:31:45,820
Huh? Where's Minami?

501
00:31:59,208 --> 00:32:00,834
I found something useful.

502
00:32:00,835 --> 00:32:02,837
It's thanks to Mr. Madoka getting hurt.

503
00:32:13,222 --> 00:32:14,973
The shed collapsed,

504
00:32:14,974 --> 00:32:18,519
injuring Mrs. Madoka's husband.

505
00:32:19,062 --> 00:32:21,063
Your position was that

506
00:32:21,064 --> 00:32:25,068
the shed belonged to you and stood
on your land, correct, Mr. Tsugihara?

507
00:32:26,653 --> 00:32:30,238
As its owner, you are liable
for damage caused by the structure.

508
00:32:30,239 --> 00:32:33,200
We will therefore seek
Mr. Madoka's medical expenses

509
00:32:33,201 --> 00:32:35,160
and compensation
for his pain and suffering,

510
00:32:35,161 --> 00:32:37,996
as well as compensation
for all lost business income

511
00:32:37,997 --> 00:32:41,083
resulting from the cafe's opening
being delayed by his injuries.

512
00:32:41,084 --> 00:32:42,335
Wait, really?

513
00:32:43,628 --> 00:32:45,380
- Yes.
- What?

514
00:32:45,880 --> 00:32:50,801
That's why I told you to remove it
promptly. Immediately. That second.

515
00:32:50,802 --> 00:32:52,261
You've got to be kidding...

516
00:32:52,845 --> 00:32:56,348
As the shed remains at risk
of further collapse,

517
00:32:56,349 --> 00:32:57,849
we demand its immediate removal.

518
00:32:57,850 --> 00:32:59,559
- Also...
- There's more?

519
00:32:59,560 --> 00:33:03,439
Yes. Earlier, while I was
in Mr. Madoka's yard,

520
00:33:04,691 --> 00:33:06,275
I found this.

521
00:33:07,068 --> 00:33:07,944
What's that?

522
00:33:08,528 --> 00:33:12,114
It's the lid of a can of paint used on
buildings and similar structures.

523
00:33:12,115 --> 00:33:15,702
I found it in the debris and investigated.

524
00:33:16,869 --> 00:33:18,121
Please take a look.

525
00:33:18,663 --> 00:33:19,621
I found

526
00:33:19,622 --> 00:33:21,456
several 18-liter cans of organic solvents.

527
00:33:21,457 --> 00:33:22,542
PAINT THINNER

528
00:33:23,751 --> 00:33:25,877
Storing these organic solvents requires

529
00:33:25,878 --> 00:33:29,381
notification or permits under
the Fire Service Act and local ordinances.

530
00:33:29,382 --> 00:33:32,300
Failure to comply carries penalties.

531
00:33:32,301 --> 00:33:35,470
Did you complete those procedures
when you inherited them from your father?

532
00:33:35,471 --> 00:33:37,973
Well, no, I...

533
00:33:37,974 --> 00:33:40,684
If you pursue your
adverse possession claim,

534
00:33:40,685 --> 00:33:42,811
we'll have to raise this in court too.

535
00:33:42,812 --> 00:33:46,314
Wait! Just a moment!

536
00:33:46,315 --> 00:33:47,441
My lawyer said

537
00:33:47,442 --> 00:33:50,277
I might get the land
without clearing the junk!

538
00:33:50,278 --> 00:33:51,445
That's...!

539
00:33:51,446 --> 00:33:54,615
Then what will you do
about your adverse possession claim?

540
00:33:56,534 --> 00:33:57,535
I'll drop it!

541
00:33:58,036 --> 00:34:01,664
Just forget the whole thing!
I'll clear away the junk too!

542
00:34:02,331 --> 00:34:05,168
I see. Understood.

543
00:34:16,137 --> 00:34:17,221
Minami.

544
00:34:20,850 --> 00:34:22,226
Thank you.

545
00:34:24,854 --> 00:34:25,896
Yeah.

546
00:34:25,897 --> 00:34:27,564
<i>Minami to the Minamida!</i>

547
00:34:27,565 --> 00:34:29,192
<i>Ririi to the Madoka!</i>

548
00:34:34,363 --> 00:34:38,576
I'll never forget how you saved my family.

549
00:34:46,209 --> 00:34:48,336
Shall we go, then?

550
00:34:48,920 --> 00:34:50,838
I've got things to do here. You go ahead.

551
00:34:51,547 --> 00:34:52,881
See you, then.

552
00:34:52,882 --> 00:34:53,966
See you.

553
00:34:55,176 --> 00:34:56,219
Oh, wait a second.

554
00:34:58,888 --> 00:35:00,139
Oh... Yes?

555
00:35:25,289 --> 00:35:26,415
Shall we go?

556
00:35:42,723 --> 00:35:46,894
I hear this area is famous
for its beautiful sunsets.

557
00:35:48,479 --> 00:35:49,647
Sunsets?

558
00:35:50,439 --> 00:35:51,440
I didn't know that.

559
00:35:53,484 --> 00:35:54,776
That's strange.

560
00:35:54,777 --> 00:35:57,196
That's what Ririi told me...

561
00:36:04,871 --> 00:36:06,330
Ms. Minamida.

562
00:36:09,625 --> 00:36:11,043
Would you like...

563
00:36:11,627 --> 00:36:12,795
to watch the sunset?

564
00:36:26,684 --> 00:36:29,520
Do you like sunsets, Minato?

565
00:36:31,606 --> 00:36:32,523
Yes.

566
00:36:33,482 --> 00:36:35,234
Well, they're beautiful, aren't they?

567
00:36:39,197 --> 00:36:40,655
Sunsets look red

568
00:36:40,656 --> 00:36:42,908
because the sun is near the horizon.

569
00:36:42,909 --> 00:36:46,453
Its light travels through
more atmosphere than during the day,

570
00:36:46,454 --> 00:36:48,788
so the blue light scatters
before reaching us,

571
00:36:48,789 --> 00:36:52,460
leaving only the red light to reach us.
I read that in a book.

572
00:36:54,045 --> 00:36:56,422
I'd never thought about why.

573
00:36:59,467 --> 00:37:02,303
It's a big lake, isn't it?

574
00:37:04,764 --> 00:37:06,807
Maybe there are whales in it.

575
00:37:09,852 --> 00:37:11,229
No, I guess not.

576
00:37:19,987 --> 00:37:21,948
Apparently, long before we moved here,

577
00:37:22,448 --> 00:37:24,199
you could see sperm whales

578
00:37:24,200 --> 00:37:26,953
if you went offshore from my hometown.

579
00:37:28,120 --> 00:37:30,248
Have you ever actually seen one?

580
00:37:30,748 --> 00:37:32,667
No, I haven't.

581
00:37:33,209 --> 00:37:35,628
I don't remember that time either.

582
00:37:37,129 --> 00:37:38,172
Someday...

583
00:37:38,798 --> 00:37:40,549
I hope you get to see a whale.

584
00:37:43,219 --> 00:37:46,055
Yes. I'd like to see one someday.

585
00:37:53,145 --> 00:37:54,188
Um...

586
00:37:55,856 --> 00:37:57,316
Ms. Minamida.

587
00:38:01,279 --> 00:38:04,115
What are you going to do now?

588
00:38:06,575 --> 00:38:08,160
Go home by car.

589
00:38:09,870 --> 00:38:11,289
That's not what I meant...

590
00:38:12,665 --> 00:38:16,836
Are you really... going to stop
being a lawyer?

591
00:38:21,215 --> 00:38:24,635
Being taken off that last case

592
00:38:25,469 --> 00:38:28,347
may have shaken your confidence.

593
00:38:28,973 --> 00:38:30,057
But

594
00:38:30,933 --> 00:38:35,771
I think you're an excellent lawyer.

595
00:38:43,154 --> 00:38:44,739
An excellent lawyer?

596
00:38:45,239 --> 00:38:46,866
Why do you think that?

597
00:38:48,701 --> 00:38:51,787
You work so hard for your clients

598
00:38:52,330 --> 00:38:55,499
that you lose sight of everything else.

599
00:38:56,542 --> 00:39:00,796
Well... Sometimes that does worry me.

600
00:39:03,007 --> 00:39:05,217
But I'm sure

601
00:39:05,760 --> 00:39:10,139
your clients find that
incredibly reassuring.

602
00:39:11,474 --> 00:39:14,727
I think standing by your clients like that

603
00:39:15,227 --> 00:39:18,189
is an important part of being a lawyer.

604
00:39:33,245 --> 00:39:34,288
Minato,

605
00:39:36,082 --> 00:39:37,625
thank you.

606
00:39:40,252 --> 00:39:43,422
I've left the firm,

607
00:39:44,423 --> 00:39:46,049
but if there's something I can do,

608
00:39:46,050 --> 00:39:49,178
I intend to keep doing my best
as a lawyer in my own way.

609
00:39:51,263 --> 00:39:52,515
I see.

610
00:39:53,099 --> 00:39:54,183
I'm glad...

611
00:40:00,815 --> 00:40:01,816
If...

612
00:40:02,775 --> 00:40:04,026
If I...

613
00:40:05,694 --> 00:40:10,658
If there's anything I can do to help,

614
00:40:12,910 --> 00:40:19,458
I'd like to keep supporting you.

615
00:40:38,727 --> 00:40:39,561
Come in.

616
00:40:39,562 --> 00:40:40,646
Excuse me!

617
00:40:53,951 --> 00:40:55,077
It's been a while.

618
00:40:56,036 --> 00:40:57,121
It's been a while.

619
00:40:57,830 --> 00:41:01,542
I'm glad your friend's problem
seems to be resolved.

620
00:41:02,042 --> 00:41:03,544
Yes. I'm glad too.

621
00:41:04,378 --> 00:41:06,630
So?

622
00:41:08,299 --> 00:41:10,384
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

623
00:41:11,760 --> 00:41:13,429
Isn't this what you came to discuss?

624
00:41:14,096 --> 00:41:16,764
Yes. I came to discuss that.

625
00:41:16,765 --> 00:41:20,186
Ririi said something about it.
Was there a problem with my letter?

626
00:41:20,686 --> 00:41:25,607
You can't just leave a resignation letter
on your supervisor's desk.

627
00:41:25,608 --> 00:41:30,154
I can't process it without speaking to you
and confirming your intentions.

628
00:41:32,031 --> 00:41:33,782
So? What will you do?

629
00:41:34,408 --> 00:41:35,909
Are you really quitting?

630
00:41:35,910 --> 00:41:39,704
Does that mean I can still quit quitting?

631
00:41:39,705 --> 00:41:42,248
Well, if you quit quitting,

632
00:41:42,249 --> 00:41:45,085
I'll deduct those days
from your paid leave.

633
00:41:46,462 --> 00:41:47,379
Then...

634
00:41:49,715 --> 00:41:50,716
I quit!

635
00:41:53,594 --> 00:41:55,596
I see. So you're quitting?

636
00:42:03,270 --> 00:42:10,236
ATTORNEY
MINAMI MINAMIDA

637
00:42:35,928 --> 00:42:38,180
How was Ms. Minamida's hometown?

638
00:42:38,973 --> 00:42:40,891
It was a long way away.

639
00:42:42,935 --> 00:42:45,436
Hey, did you hear anything

640
00:42:45,437 --> 00:42:48,524
about her family owning
a lot of land or something?

641
00:42:49,024 --> 00:42:49,857
No.

642
00:42:49,858 --> 00:42:51,151
I see.

643
00:42:53,362 --> 00:42:54,904
Why do you ask?

644
00:42:54,905 --> 00:42:57,156
Something doesn't sit right

645
00:42:57,157 --> 00:42:59,784
about how the managing partner
treats Ms. Minamida.

646
00:42:59,785 --> 00:43:02,829
The other day, she kept going on
about teamwork.

647
00:43:02,830 --> 00:43:04,665
That's not like her, is it?

648
00:43:05,249 --> 00:43:06,457
Are you jealous?

649
00:43:06,458 --> 00:43:07,834
Of course not.

650
00:43:07,835 --> 00:43:11,838
She has a disability.
I understand making some allowances.

651
00:43:11,839 --> 00:43:13,798
But even so...

652
00:43:13,799 --> 00:43:18,970
Maybe Ms. Minamida has some
seriously powerful connections.

653
00:43:18,971 --> 00:43:20,055
Mr. Himi.

654
00:43:21,557 --> 00:43:22,850
You must have time to spare.

655
00:43:25,436 --> 00:43:26,603
No, I don't!

656
00:43:26,604 --> 00:43:29,105
I've got a meeting over a meal
with a publisher later!

657
00:43:29,106 --> 00:43:30,316
Hello?

658
00:43:30,941 --> 00:43:34,570
I thought you might have been
looking out for Minami...

659
00:43:35,237 --> 00:43:38,115
I'm glad she's decided to stay.

660
00:43:42,703 --> 00:43:43,996
You know,

661
00:43:44,580 --> 00:43:46,332
I think very highly of her abilities.

662
00:43:46,915 --> 00:43:49,751
She seems very persistent with her cases.

663
00:43:49,752 --> 00:43:51,502
And she's very creative.

664
00:43:51,503 --> 00:43:55,298
<i>I think the other lawyers
could learn something from her.</i>

665
00:43:55,299 --> 00:43:56,842
I'm glad to hear you say that...

666
00:43:57,509 --> 00:44:00,804
But if she ever causes you any trouble,

667
00:44:01,305 --> 00:44:03,056
- don't hesitate to tell me.
<i>- Don't worry.</i>

668
00:44:03,057 --> 00:44:06,351
She may still have a lot to learn,

669
00:44:06,352 --> 00:44:07,978
but that will come with time.

670
00:44:08,854 --> 00:44:11,397
Don't worry. Leave it to me.

671
00:44:11,398 --> 00:44:12,941
Thank you.

672
00:44:13,609 --> 00:44:15,318
I can't thank you enough.

673
00:44:15,319 --> 00:44:18,155
<i>All right, then. Call me anytime.</i>

674
00:44:25,079 --> 00:44:26,121
MINAMI MINAMIDA

675
00:44:32,711 --> 00:44:33,921
Like mother, like daughter.

676
00:44:36,173 --> 00:44:37,883
She's just like her mother.

677
00:44:44,765 --> 00:44:49,769
Subtitle translation by: Hasan Hüseyin
Öztürk

678
00:44:49,770 --> 00:44:52,688
I'll fight this to the bitter end,
however long it takes!

679
00:44:52,689 --> 00:44:55,525
Is this really someone
who would slander another person?

680
00:44:55,526 --> 00:44:58,027
<i>You don't need to do anything this time,
Ms. Minamida.</i>

681
00:44:58,028 --> 00:44:59,821
<i>I can't let myself fall behind either.</i>

682
00:44:59,822 --> 00:45:01,614
<i>You watched the sunset together, right?</i>

683
00:45:01,615 --> 00:45:02,740
Tell me!

684
00:45:02,741 --> 00:45:04,076
I'm not telling!

685
00:45:04,785 --> 00:45:06,954
- Mr. Himi?
- Curious?

686
00:45:09,540 --> 00:45:12,708
"Minato Funai likes Minami Minamida."
Is that true?

687
00:45:12,709 --> 00:45:13,794
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION
